{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And it was when Moses came down.</b> On the third day, on the Sabbath, the tenth of Tishrei, after forty days, the third set." "<b>And the two tablets of the testimony.</b> What is missing here is the making of the ark that Moses made — Scripture explains it in the portion of Eikev, and in it they were until the first of Nisan, when the Tabernacle and all its vessels were anointed, and they placed them in the ark that Betzalel made." "<b>And Moses did not know that the skin of his face had become radiant.</b> When HaShem placed His hand over the opening of the cave in which Moses was, as it is written, ״והיה בעבור כבודי ושמתיך בנקרת הצור ושכותי כפי עליך עד עברי״, and it is written, ״ויעבר ה׳ על פניו״ — from there he merited the horns of splendor. And the reason he merited this with the latter tablets and not the first ones is that the first ones were given in the view of all, with thunder and sounds and fire, whereas concerning these it is written, ״גם איש אל ירא בכל ההר״ וגו׳. And since the first ones were given with sounds and lightning and cloud and torches, while these were given in secret — were it not for the horns of splendor, the nations would have an opening to say that other tablets were not given, and they would not have believed that HaShem gave them to him. Another interpretation: because they wanted to appoint a leader for themselves in place of Moses, HaShem showed them that he is filled with the splendor of His Shekhinah on his face, and it is not fitting to appoint another in his place."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:58.455919195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}